{
  "title": "zxing-wasm vs. Dynamsoft Barcode Reader vs. Scandit — JavaScript/WASM",
  "dataset": "BarBeR public dataset",
  "disclosure": "This benchmark compares three JavaScript/WASM barcode readers on the public third-party BarBeR dataset. Dynamsoft, the developer of Dynamsoft Barcode Reader, built and published this benchmark; Scandit and ZXing are third-party products evaluated with their standard, publicly documented settings. Scandit runs in BarcodeBatch (MatrixScan) mode over a single ImageFrameSource frame per image, with all BarBeR-relevant symbologies enabled; it has no JAPAN_POST or POSTNET symbology, so those annotations are scored as unsupported_format (no-read), the same treatment zxing-wasm gets for formats it does not support. Scandit reports EAN-13 and UPC-A as one combined symbology, which the harness splits by payload length; all Code 128 results are labeled CODE_128 rather than GS1_128 because BarBeR annotates 1,120 Code 128 barcodes as CODE_128 and only 4 as GS1_128 (the pre-correction records are retained for audit). To make the comparison auditable, the protocol, decoder configurations, environment details, dataset manifest, HTML report, and per-image raw results are provided. BarBeR's standardized annotations were generated with assistance from proprietary Datalogic software. Difficult undecodable barcode regions are excluded from decoding accuracy when no reliable payload is available.",
